host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The manual room takes the system name
prompt Keaton said kg to all recommendations, which was four renames one per round in cost order. This is the first and smallest -- manual/glow-os becomes manual/grain-os.
think Measured first: 5 tracked files, 173 occurrences of the name across 89 files, 16 living and 73 dated. manual/grain-os was free.
think Then found the trap before it bit. Most of those 173 occurrences sit INSIDE dated filenames -- 20260720-223226_glow-os-shape-not-mold.md and 20260713-235455_keaton-name-and-glow-os-umbrella.md. A blanket glow-os to grain-os would have corrupted every reference to two real dated artifacts whose names can never change.
think So the sweep matched `manual/glow-os` rather than `glow-os`, which is the same discipline the crux round needed for the opposite reason: there the WORD had to survive and the path moved, here the FILENAME has to survive and the directory moves. A rename is always a question of which occurrences mean the thing being renamed.
obs Fourteen occurrences repointed across 7 living files, one prose room-list fixed, and 30 dated files left holding the elder path exactly as written. Twenty-seven guards green on the first pass, which is what a measured sweep buys.
obs The room was named for Glow, the rune language, while its actual job is teaching a reader the system, whose name is Grain. The elder name sent every newcomer to the wrong noun on their first click. Glow keeps its name in every file where the language is genuinely the subject.
obs Committed the cairn in the same commit as the move rather than ahead of it. For a breach that is honest -- nothing is rewritten, so the walk-back nib stays reachable on both remotes either way. A deep debride is the case where the cairn must land first, because there the walk-back goes unreachable.
loom rename files_moved=5 name_occurrences=173 files_holding=89 living_repointed=14 living_files=7 testimony_untouched=30 guards_red=0
file manual/grain-os/ the onboarding room, renamed from manual/glow-os/
file construction/CAIRNS.md the walk-back, with why the name moved
recommend keep-going -- rename two of four is cairn to checkpoint, and it wants doing before the rest because every later rename records its walk-back in that ledger. Then Skate to Surf with Surf Social, then the name change as a deep debride last, so one history rewrite covers everything.
